WEBVTT

00:00:01.281 --> 00:00:02.994
Jerusalem has fallen.

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:06.791
Far from home, the prophet Ezekiel
sees a temple in a vision.

00:00:08.817 --> 00:00:10.872
A guide with a measuring reed

00:00:10.872 --> 00:00:13.835
leads him through its gates,
measuring as they go.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.393
We're picturing that account here.

00:00:18.809 --> 00:00:20.569
Its measurements guide us;

00:00:20.569 --> 00:00:23.254
some details are an artist's interpretation.

00:00:24.793 --> 00:00:27.107
In the inner court stands an altar,

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.256
with steps facing east,
before the sanctuary.

00:00:32.728 --> 00:00:35.089
The vision carries a promise for Israel:

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.126
God will dwell among his people.

00:00:40.765 --> 00:00:43.913
Inside, carved timber surrounds
a wooden altar,

00:00:44.117 --> 00:00:46.413
described as the table before the Lord.

00:00:48.604 --> 00:00:51.215
Palms alternate with cherubim,

00:00:51.215 --> 00:00:55.224
each bearing two faces:
a human and a young lion.

00:00:56.362 --> 00:00:59.649
Then water emerges beneath the threshold.

00:00:59.973 --> 00:01:02.288
In Ezekiel's vision, it becomes a river

00:01:02.427 --> 00:01:03.612
that brings life.

